WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.470
Dissolve some sodium
ethanoate in pure water.

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.570
No sodium hydroxide goes in.

3
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.790
No alkali of any kind.

4
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.490
Yet test the solution,
and its pH is above 7.

5
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:12.890
It's alkaline.

6
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.950
Why is a solution of sodium ethanoate
alkaline, when no hydroxide was put in?

7
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.130
In this mission, you'll calculate
the pH of weak acids and weak bases,

8
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.130
using two approximations,
so no quadratic is needed.

9
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.850
You'll find out why some
salts give acidic solutions,

10
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.490
some give basic ones,
and some are neutral.

11
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.910
Your mission: explain why sodium
ethanoate solution is alkaline.
